# File: scripts/__tests__/jest-per-test-coverage.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/590-make-per-test-coverage-outcome-ids-independent-of-the-test-file-so-the-test-layer-gate-can-accept-cross-file-conversions/requirements.md
Feature: Make per-test coverage outcome ids independent of the test file so the test-layer gate can accept cross-file conversions

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Outcome ids do not depend on the test file
    Given Jest results for two test files that each contain an it titled the same under different describe blocks
    When collect derives each file's report entry
    Then both entries report the identical outcome "<it title>:<status>"
    And no reported outcome contains a test file path or a describe title
    And a suite that fails to run reports the outcome "(suite):failed"

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A cross-file doc to bdd conversion passes the gate
    Given a doc test file whose it blocks were moved into an @SCN-tagged bdd test in another file covering the same lines and branches
    When the original file is deleted and gateBatch evaluates its batch with bdd kept
    Then the batch is accepted
    And its deleted evidence lists the removed test with the bdd test id in coveredBy and the removed test's lines

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Dropping an asserted outcome is still refused
    Given the same conversion with one moved it block missing from the bdd test
    When gateBatch evaluates the batch
    Then it is refused with test_layers_coverage_gap
    And gap.outcomes lists exactly the missing outcome

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Candidates label a cross-file covered test as duplicate
    Given coverage for a doc test and for a bdd test in another file whose lines, branches and outcomes include the doc test's
    When computeCandidates runs with bdd kept
    Then the doc test is labelled duplicate with the bdd test id in coveredBy
